| `capabilities/` | Reviewed durable capabilities, capability maps, and local memory. | Do not store unreviewed temporary workflows here. |
| `publication/` | Public profile, bio, positioning, website, articles, and public claims. | Every public claim must trace back to evidence. |
| `integrations/` | GitHub, Feishu/Lark, Hermes, and data source config. | Do not store secrets; use larkcli for Feishu/Lark operations. |
| `security/` | Banned material, publication policy, and secret boundaries. | Read before publishing or syncing. |
| `governance/` | Instance-level schemas, policies, and decisions. | Stores governance decisions, not private source bodies. |

## Continuous Evolution Loop

```text
sources / metabolism
-> runtime/sessions
-> runtime/runtime-skills
-> runtime/runtime-lessons
-> evolution/ipo
-> capabilities / meta-skills
```

1. Approved material enters `sources/` or `metabolism/inbox/` with purpose and boundaries.
2. InnerAtlas/Wenxin produces identity artifacts: who I am, where I stand, what is missing, and where I may go.
3. PSP XML distills value ordering, judgment style, operating axes, delegation boundary, and behavior boundaries.
4. Taste Generator updates `taste/`, `DESIGN_TASTE.xml`, and `DESIGN.md`.
5. Real work enters `runtime/sessions/` and creates runtime skills and lessons.
6. IPO Reverse reconstructs evidence, hidden cognitive tasks, middle artifacts, and reusable IPO from finished outputs.
7. After owner alignment, stable capabilities move into `capabilities/` or `meta-skills/skills/`.

## AI Usage

Read `AGENT.md` and `artifacts/current.yml` first. For facts, source material, publication boundaries, or long-term claims, route into `sources/`, `identity/`, `taste/`, `runtime/`, `publication/`, and `security/` as needed.

`AGENT.md` is this instance's agent entrypoint, not an installable Codex Skill. Real self-evolution Skills live under `evolution/organ-systems/*/SKILL.md`; stable capability Skills live under `capabilities/*/SKILL.md` or an external skill package.

## Public Boundary

This repo must not store secrets, passwords, contracts, financial data, IDs, customer details, raw meeting transcripts, private chat logs, or private wiki bodies.

The public surface contains only owner-approved derived content; private collaboration contains trusted shared memory; local/server authority keeps raw sensitive material.
